Does the quantile estimation mechanism described below satisfy $\varepsilon$-differential privacy?

\begin{algorithm}[H]
\caption{DP Single Quantile Estimation via Exponential Mechanism}
\KwIn{Quantile level $q\in[0,1]$, dataset $X = (x_1,\ldots,x_n) \subset (a,b)^n$, privacy budget $\varepsilon$.}
\KwOut{Quantile estimate $v \in (a,b)$.}

Define: $u(X,w) = -\bigl|\#\{x \in X \mid x<w\} - \lfloor qn \rfloor \bigl|$ \\
